From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: keep fault completion independent of recovery's GPU lock

The recovery worker holds gpu->lock while dropping its runtime-PM reference.
GMU shutdown can then wait for fault_coredump_done after an OOB timeout. The
SMMU fault thread must complete that event, but its optional crash-state capture
currently waits for the same GPU lock. Neither side can proceed.

Skip the optional capture when the lock is busy. Keep ordinary fault reporting,
the handler's completion and SMMU resume path, and uncontended capture intact.
This removes the recovery lock cycle; it does not prevent the original GPU fault.

Compared with upstream Linux 90b754d40117 and the Uke GPU fault/worker stacks.
The actual-function host fixture reproduces the blocking cycle before this
change and checks ordinary capture, duplicate handling and cleanup afterward.

Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -597,7 +597,9 @@ void msm_gpu_fault_crashstate_capture(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct msm_gpu_fault_info *fault_info)
 	char *comm = NULL, *cmd = NULL;
 	unsigned int noreclaim_flag;
 
-	mutex_lock(&gpu->lock);
+	/* Recovery may hold this lock while waiting for our fault completion. */
+	if (!mutex_trylock(&gpu->lock))
+		return;
 
 	submit = find_submit(cur_ring, cur_ring->memptrs->fence + 1);
 	if (submit && submit->fault_dumped)
